179/Protocol BO44178 , Version 4 RENAL EVENTS  
Eligible patients must have adequate renal function.  Renal function, including serum 
creatinine, should be monitored throughout study treatment.  Participant s with abnormal 
renal function should be evaluated and treated for other more common etiologies 
(including prerenal and postrenal causes, and concomitant medications such as non -
steroidal ant i-inflammatory drugs).  Refer the participant to a renal speciali st if clinically 
indicated.  A  renal biopsy may be required to enable a definitive diagnosis and 
appropriate treatment.  
Participants with signs and symptoms of nephritis, in the absence of an identified 
alternate etiology, should be treated according to the guidelines in Table  A6-13. 
  

